b.constraint('requirement_facade_non_authority',['requirement_declaration'],'Declarations may reference requirement algebra hooks/projections but cannot emit events, write ledgers, choose traversal, close assurance or own continuation/re-entry. Facades expose carriers/constructors only and cannot admit events, project runtime truth, bind evidence, fold assurance, residualize pressure, select continuation or route re-entry.',[(0,39,41)])
b.constraint('lifecycle_routes_inert',['requirement_route'],'Lifecycle composition carries route/contract refs, symbolic bindings and digests without importing, instantiating or depending on ABG runtime modules. Named ABG route reference does not confer authority; resolution occurs only when HoG reaches it and ABG checks admitted route/publication authority. Reject unknown routes, missing contracts, malformed digests, duplicate composition refs and runtime-state/event-authority smuggling.',[(0,43,47)])
b.constraint('existing_requirement_graph_kernel',['requirement_declaration','requirement_route'],'Express parent/child, refinement, dependency, obstruction, mitigation, satisfaction, evidence, assurance and proof-evidence structure through existing RequirementTerm and typed relations. No second KAOS/goal/decomposition/obstacle/requirement-graph kernel or Product test policy from proof-role labels. Parent/child/refinement may name routes but cannot import runtime modules, mint admitted refs, emit events/project folds/residualize/select continuation/route re-entry.',[(0,49,53)])
