b.constraint('selection_structural_nonchoice',['selection_boundary'],'The interpreter may enumerate lawful candidates but cannot silently choose the best. Candidate families preserve one explicit outer contract for every lawful candidate. Policy hints are visible to evaluators/consumers, not executable semantics. A published GraphFunction bound by Job is callable work, not an implicit candidate-family alternative.',[(9,21,29)])
b.latitude('selection_exposure',['selection_boundary'],['Expose candidate families, interface equivalence, tags and policy hints.','Use deterministic rule execution, probabilistic contextual analysis, human judgment or higher intent/business logic to make declared selection.'],['Hidden workflow choice, business-priority or engine strategy in GTL.'],[(9,17,27)])
b.constraint('selection_declared_execution',['selection_boundary'],'Applicability, evaluation and selection are declared graph computations traversed by HoG. Findings/choices cross ABG admission before consequence/advancement. Overlays, plugins, SDKs and downstream controllers cannot implement rival selection/continuation loops. Policy remains explicit work above the interpreter.',[(9,31,36)])
b.constraint('selection_policy_contract',['selection_boundary'],'Executable policy binds evaluator, required frame/input contracts, criteria and consequence relation. Weights/thresholds prioritize only permitted choices and cannot waive mandatory constraints, required independent evaluation or reserved owner rulings. Hints alone are insufficient.',[(9,38,42)])
b.constraint('selection_regime_law',['selection_boundary'],'Every evaluator declares its regime. Supplied F_D implements an explicit total rule on a closed declared domain; where no such rule exists F_P owns contextual judgment. Both preserve evidence/result contracts and admission boundary; deterministic implementation itself conveys no semantic authority.',[(9,44,48)])
b.constraint('registered_choice_support',['registered_governance_selection'],'In selected 5.0 governance choose only Program-permitted preregistered callables from the exact admitted catalog view. Each graph declares functional purpose/use conditions linked to input/result/effect contracts. Selection identifies that declaration, inputs, reason and evidence. Purpose or catalog presence alone proves neither applicability, permission nor completion. Missing suitable capability or unresolved required support stays an explicit gap.',[(9,50,57)])
b.constraint('registered_choice_change_boundary',['registered_governance_selection'],'Changed evidence may change a registered choice or justify compatible result reuse while conserving original outcome, unaffected valid work and remaining obligations. It cannot author/recompose definitions, silently rewrite running Program or expand callable scope. Existing registered-template materialization and recursion remain lawful. Future graph-building is outside this increment under Product Release Boundaries.',[(9,58,63)],exceptions=['Existing registered-template materialization and recursive invocation remain lawful.'])
